ce I  finally got to the point where I was  able to audition and read with him then  we just both kind of looked at each  other we were like wow we were literally  out that night and we became fast  friends  audiences fell hard for 2004's The  Notebook but according to the director  the drama sometimes continued after he  yelled cut co-stars Rachel McAdams and  Ryan Gosling apparently  in front of the entire crew nick  cassavetes told vh1 they were really not  getting along one day on set Brian came  to me and there's 150 people standing in  this big scene and he says would you  take her out of here and bring in  another actress to read off-camera with  me  I can't I can't do it with her I'm just  not getting anything from this now I  hate you useful producers called to  clear the air meaning after Gosselin  refused to shoot the big scene with  McAdams and it got off to a rocky start  the director explained they started  screaming and yelling at each other they  had it out I think Ryan respected her  for standing up for her character and  Rachel was happy to get that out in the  open  the rest of the film wasn't smooth  sailing but it was smoother sailing the  two actors ended up dating for a couple  of years after wrapping the notebook  rumors about a beef between Vin Diesel  and the fate of the Furious co-star  Dwayne Johnson turned out to be 100%  true it all kicked off when Johnson took  to social media to slam an anonymous  co-star during the last week of filming  sane in a since deleted Instagram  caption my female co-stars are always  amazing and I love them my male co-stars  however are a different story some  conduct themselves a stand-up men and  true professionals while others don't  the ones that don't are too chicken to  do anything about it anyway candy-asses  Johnson later confirmed that he was  indeed talking about Diesel who was  reportedly late to set on a regular  basis Johnson later told Rolling Stone  then and I had a few discussions  including 